To display text in columns within a TextField in Adobe Animate (formerly Flash) using ActionScript 3.0, you can create a custom function to format the text. However, TextFields in Adobe Animate do not natively support columnar text display. You can simulate columns by splitting the text into multiple lines and then adjusting the TextField's properties to display them side by side.

Here's a basic example of how you might achieve a columnar text effect:

```actionscript
import flash.text.TextField;
import flash.text.TextFieldAutoSize;
import flash.text.TextFormat;

// Create a new TextField
var textField:TextField = new TextField();
textField.autoSize = TextFieldAutoSize.LEFT;

// Set the text format
var format:TextFormat = new TextFormat();
format.font = "Arial";
format.size = 12;

// Set the text for the TextField
textField.defaultTextFormat = format;
textField.text = "This is a sample text that will be displayed in columns. " +
                 "You can adjust the width of the TextField to see the columns effect.";

// Set the width of the TextField to simulate columns
textField.width = 200; // Adjust this value to change the number of columns

// Add the TextField to the stage
addChild(textField);
```

In this example, you can adjust the `textField.width` property to change the number of columns. The text will be displayed in a single column, but you can manually set the width to create a visual effect of columns. For a more advanced columnar text effect, you would need to write a custom function to split the text into multiple lines and position them accordingly, which can be quite complex and may not be fully supported by the TextField component.

For a more sophisticated text layout, consider using a third-party library or a different approach, such as creating a custom component that can handle multi-column text rendering.

